{"id": "EUVD-2026-101137", "enisaUuid": "d8d05057-fbed-3ed7-bf37-6695a27a038a", "description": "libsmb2 through 6.2 contains an integer underflow vulnerability in decode_acl that allows malicious SMB servers to trigger heap out-of-bounds reads via crafted security descriptors. Attackers controlling a server or intercepting unsigned sessions can send an AclSize below 8 in a QUERY_INFO reply, bypassing ACE bounds checks and crashing the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:29:23", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libsmb2-query-info-reply-oob-read", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/blob/d67e213a5c4e7e4969fd81f0b95e4ca5831fbba1/lib/smb2-data-security-descriptor.c#L266", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/commit/523abe20be3207011a936db47f1d3bab79c05450", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libsmb2-through-6.2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-decode-acl-integer-underflow"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110714", "GHSA-f7hf-m5cf-j6wv"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.55, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4dd4240b-afe0-3e5c-971f-f631db34d014", "product": {"name": "libsmb2", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "634329e0-fa78-398c-b27d-65bcce71d94c", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}], "isExploited": false}